{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/483922-a-question-about-staking","id":483922,"title":"A Question About Staking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-17T15:25:30-07:00","id":483922,"title":"A Question About Staking","content":"So I am getting back into White Wolf games... And I'll admit I am not fond of the new 2nd Edition stuff...<br /> <br /> But here is my question:<br /> <br /> If a Vampire is staked, as in an attack is made at the -3 penalty, and 5 successes (or more) are achieved on the roll can the Vampire spend blood in reflex to the damage to reduce the damage to below 5 and thus prevent the staking from knocking the bloodsucker into Torpor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5721-hwalsh","name":"HWalsh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T15:29:11-07:00","id":483942,"title":"","content":"If you've got Resilience, you can prevent it. Otherwise, you're healing damage after it's done, which you won't be able to do in torpor.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry to hear you aren't fond of the 2nd edition stuff. Do you feel like explaining why? I've seen a lot of people with misgivings that were laboring under misconceptions about it, and if we can clear those up for you, it might hopefully make it easier for you to enjoy the 2nd edition games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T15:31:01-07:00","id":483944,"title":"","content":"Technically, yes. In my games I'd probably rule no for dramatic purposes. Resistance also works as a method to circumvent a staking by ignoring damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T15:35:02-07:00","id":483967,"title":"","content":"The actual damage doesn't really matter, it's just a mechanical check for &quot;yep, it's in.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think you can heal a wound that's got the inflicting implement stuck in it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}